<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Rimba Apparel — WhatsApp Connection</title>
  <% if (status === 'qr_pending' || status === 'connecting' || status === 'reconnecting' || status === 'disconnected') { %>
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="5">
  <% } %>
  <style>
    body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; background: #f6f5f2; margin: 0; color: #2b2b2b; }
    header { background: #2b2b2b; color: #fff; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; }
    header h1 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0; }
    main { max-width: 560px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
    .card { background: #fff; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); text-align: center; }
    .risk-notice { background: #fff3cd; color: #664d03; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-align: left; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    .risk-notice strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
    .status-box { padding: 1rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; text-align: left; }
    .status-open { background: #eaf7ea; color: #1e7d1e; }
    .status-qr { background: #e7f3ff; color: #0b5fb0; }
    .status-warn { background: #ffe4e4; color: #b3261e; }
    .status-neutral { background: #f0f0f0; color: #555; }
    img.qr { max-width: 280px; width: 100%; border: 1px solid #eee; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.5rem; background: #fff; }
    form.reset-form { margin-top: 1rem; }
    button { padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem; background: #2b2b2b; color: #fff; border: none; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.95rem; cursor: pointer; }
    button:hover { background: #444; }
    a.back-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: #555; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>Rimba Apparel — WhatsApp Connection</h1>
  </header>
  <main>
    <div class="card">
      <% if (whatsappMode !== 'baileys') { %>
        <div class="status-box status-neutral">
          <strong>Baileys mode is not active.</strong>
          <p>This app is currently running in <strong>Cloud API mode</strong>
          (<code>WHATSAPP_MODE=cloud_api</code>), using Meta's official
          WhatsApp Cloud API. There is no pairing step in this mode — the
          business's WhatsApp number is connected via the Meta App
          dashboard instead.</p>
        </div>
      <% } else { %>
        <!--
          NFR-303 (Honesty): this disclosure is shown on every load while
          Baileys mode is active, not just once at setup, and not buried
          in a code comment or README-only footnote.
        -->
        <div class="risk-notice">
          <strong>Ban-risk trade-off — please read before pairing</strong>
          Baileys connects using an unofficial, reverse-engineered
          WhatsApp protocol — not Meta's official Cloud API. WhatsApp does
          not support or sanction this. The connected number carries a
          real risk of being banned or rate-limited, even for a
          reply-only usage pattern like this app's. Use a number you are
          willing to lose — not the business owner's primary/personal
          number — and treat this as a lower-cost, higher-risk tier
          compared to the official Cloud API.
        </div>

        <% if (status === 'open') { %>
          <div class="status-box status-open">
            <strong>Connected.</strong> This app is paired with a WhatsApp
            number and is receiving/replying to messages automatically.
          </div>
        <% } else if (status === 'qr_pending' && qrDataUrl) { %>
          <div class="status-box status-qr">
            <strong>Scan to connect.</strong> Open WhatsApp on the phone
            you want to pair → Settings → Linked Devices → Link a Device,
            then scan this code.
          </div>
          <img class="qr" src="<%= qrDataUrl %>" alt="WhatsApp pairing QR code">
        <% } else if (status === 'reconnecting') { %>
          <div class="status-box status-neutral">
            <strong>Reconnecting…</strong> The connection dropped
            (network blip or a WhatsApp-side restart) and the app is
            automatically retrying with backoff. This page refreshes
            itself every few seconds — no action needed.
          </div>
        <% } else if (status === 'action_needed') { %>
          <div class="status-box status-warn">
            <strong>Reconnect needed.</strong>
            <%= disconnectReasonMessage || 'The WhatsApp connection cannot be automatically recovered.' %>
            The bot will <strong>not</strong> keep retrying on its
            own — retrying a session in this state is pointless — so it has
            stopped responding to messages until it's re-paired.
          </div>
          <form class="reset-form" method="POST" action="/whatsapp/pair/reset">
            <button type="submit">Generate new QR code</button>
          </form>
        <% } else { %>
          <div class="status-box status-neutral">
            <strong>Starting connection…</strong> Waiting for a QR code
            from WhatsApp. This page refreshes itself every few seconds.
          </div>
        <% } %>
      <% } %>

      <a class="back-link" href="/leads">&larr; Back to leads dashboard</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
